        "original_id": "87abba81-3354-5836-b712-74ea99c72508",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: United Kingdom, England\n- Topics: Culture of the United Kingdom, Religion in the United Kingdom\n- Concepts: Christianity, religions in the United Kingdom\n\nFacts:\n- Religion in the United Kingdom and in the states that preceded it has been dominated by various forms of Christianity for more than 1,400 years.\n- According to the 2011 Census, Christianity was the largest religion in the United Kingdom, followed by Islam, Hinduism, Sikhism, Judaism, and Buddhism by number of adherents.\n- The culture of the United Kingdom is influenced by the country's history as a developed island country, a liberal democracy, a major power, its predominantly Christian religious life, and its composition of four countries, including England.",
